  <prompt>Extend RuleSetService and RuleSetEndpoints for the four scope levels (notes/rule-set-scope-design.md sections 4.1-4.6 and 5.1, as revised by uac-r2's two reviews, section 12): validate scope and core record on create, assign and publish; require Read and AppendTo on a named core record; on every route keyed by the rule-set id, read the set's core record on the server and check the caller's Read (plus AppendTo on writes) before anything is read back or written, answering one uniform 404; lock a Published set's scope (409 ruleset.scope_locked); re-scope a Draft the way InvoiceDocumentRefile re-files (isolation read, conditional lookup write, ReparentAsync on the set with F3, AfterRefileAsync only when the parents changed); write the business-unit list; route the set, policy and version creates through IRecordOwnershipResolver with each row's own lookups as parents; file a record-scoped set's source document under that record, Restricted, owned from its own row and stored in the record's container (D-145); and add sprk_ruleset to the secure family in ONE change (lineage with entity set sprk_rulesets, OwnershipParentEntities, the client OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES list, the role row with a live refusal probe, the creator-person stamp and script entry, census Routed entries, UnscannedWriters and PersonBearingWriters, a separate non-throwing NFR-05 list), with the narrower guard and its ontology twin. Core-record delete always keeps the set, unlinked (D-146); this task adds no delete code and sends uac-r2 no citing-lookup list.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs, the Finance authorization filter, IRecordOwnershipResolver, SecureChildReconciler and the uac-r2 secure-family model.</role>

  <goal>A record-scoped rule set can be created, assigned and published only with a valid scope and core record and with the caller's Read + AppendTo on it; no route keyed by a rule-set id reveals or changes a set whose core record the caller cannot read; a Draft re-scope off a Secure record passes F3, writes nothing on any refusal, and moves the set's rows; the set, policies and versions are owned through the resolver from their own lookups (Secure team under a Secure record); a record-scoped set's source document is filed under its record, Restricted and owned from its own row; sprk_ruleset is in the lineage, the ownership parents, the client child list, the role set, the creator-person set and the census in one change, with SecureFamilyConsistencyTests, the census, RefileWriterAfterRefileGuardTests, RouteAuthorizationGuardTests and SecureChildNewCommandAgreementTests passing; the NFR-05 run reports no non-admin role reaching the Secure business unit on the three tables, and a missing privilege name never blinds the census.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design note sections 4.1-4.6, 5.1, 5.3, 12 (ontology-r1 conditions 1-2; uac-r2 review rounds 1 and 2). Decisions: D-136 / ontology D-171; D-137 / ontology D-172 (Q9 lock, no Restrict); D-141 (Q1, the S8 snapshot; Q11 answered: the set joins the secure family now); D-145 (source documents); D-146 (core-record delete always keeps the set, unlinked; supersedes D-141 Q10 and D-137's "retire if cited"). Cite symbols, not line numbers: this branch carries UAC-file edits from 013 / 026 and lacks master's #2130 changes, so line numbers drift (uac-r2 round 2, general). Current code, by symbol: RuleSetService (RuleSetScope enum, CreateAsync and its source-document create through the CreateDocumentAsync seam, ListAsync, GetAsync, AddDraftsAsync, CreateDraftRuleAsync, EditAsync and its new-version create, publish and its scope check, AssignAsync, SetVisibilityAsync, Summarize, OwnerContext with RequestedBy); RuleSetEndpoints (every route behind AddFinanceAuthorizationFilter(BillingAdminAuthorization...) only; TryParseScope; the AssignCallers reason for AssignRuleSet). UAC, by symbol: RecordOwnershipContext.ParentsOf(Entity row), RecordOwnershipResolver.OwnershipParentEntities and CitationLookups, RecordReparent.SecureExitCaller, IRecordOwnershipResolver.ReparentAsync (its applyChange callback and its ParentsUnchanged result), SecureChildReconciler.AfterRefileAsync, RefileIsolationRead.BeforeWriteAsync, SecureDesignationRemoval.IsNotPermitted and NotPermittedReasonCode ("sdap.unsecure.not_permitted"), ProblemDetailsHelper.RecordOwnerRefused, FinanceAuthorizationFilter.UniformRecordNotFound and FinanceDenial.UniformNotFound, CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerRightsForRecordsAsync, SecureChildLineage (the sprk_policy entry), the census (ChildTables, RuleSetServicePolicyWaiver, the sprk_policy / sprk_policyversion entries, UnscannedWriters, PersonBearingWriters, EveryChildTableTheServerCreatesCarriesTheCreatorPersonColumn, EveryAppCreateWriterThatActsForAPersonNamesThem), RecordCreatorPerson.StampedChildTables pinned to scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 $Tables by ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchemaAgreementTests (and $SolutionHomes, whose tables the script never creates the column for), the config/secure-record-owner-role.json sprk_policy entry (#2084 probe evidence, 0x80040299), SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion.GuardedPrivileges and RequireGuardedPrivilegesResolved (clause 1), OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/utils/adapters/bffChildWriteAdapter.ts (pinned to OwnershipParentEntities minus the roots by SecureChildNewCommandAgreementTests; ChildSubgridsOnMainForms), RecordContainerResolver, RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Ledger.cs GovernedFiles entry for Api/Finance/RuleSetEndpoints.cs. Role XML: Spaarke Basic User / Core User hold prvReadsprk_ruleset at Deep (SpaarkeMaster Roles); prvWritesprk_ruleset (BillingAdminAuthorization) is held through a role not in SpaarkeMaster source. uac-r2 #2143 is tracked as #2150: ReparentAsync becomes a conditional update on RowVersion with at most 3 retries and a typed fail-closed refusal (RecordOwnerUnsettledException, 409 record_owner_unsettled, not merged at authoring). UAC T7 (notes/2119-manage-access-all-forms-design.md §6 on work/unified-access-control-r2; owner accepted D7 in UAC round 110): every external document surface hides a document whose own sprk_accesspermission is Restricted. uac-r2's delete design: projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/core-record-delete-design.md §12 (3fbf650fb): the delete job always unlinks R's own rule set (with its policies and versions) and never deletes or re-owns it.</background>
