    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Core-record check on a finance route" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/RateCardImportEndpoints.cs (the FinanceAuthorizationCheck per query id)">Query ids, one FinanceAuthorizationCheck per id on the Record path, operation key per check.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Owner routed with parents" location="RateCardImportService.ImportAsync (ResolveOwnerAsync with ForParents); RecordOwnershipContext.ParentsOf(row)">ForParents(parents, caller) with RequestedBy; refusal writes nothing.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Re-file with F3 and the after-re-file step" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceDocumentRefile.cs">BeforeWriteAsync (503 on failure), ReparentAsync with SecureExitCaller and a conditional applyChange, IsNotPermitted mapping, AfterRefileAsync when !ParentsUnchanged.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Reconciler test fixture" location="tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Access/SecureChildReconcilerGateDecisionRecordTests.cs, TestInfrastructure/SecureChildReconcilerFixtures.cs">Copy for the three-hop test.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Role row with probe evidence" location="config/secure-record-owner-role.json (the sprk_policy and sprk_policyversion entries, #2084)">Reason plus verbatim refusal.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">git fetch; git merge origin/master (including #2150 when it lands); git merge-base --is-ancestor of the #2150 fix and of UAC T7 against HEAD (STOP if either is missing); read notes/080-ruleset-scope-schema.md for the live names and values; confirm ontology-r1's sprk_createdbyperson on sprk_policy and sprk_policyversion exists (metadata read).</step>
    <step order="1">RuleSetScope gains Record = 100000002 and FirmRecord = 100000003; Summarize and TryParseScope name them.</step>
    <step order="2">Validation matrix (4.1) on create, assign, publish; query-parameter inputs; BU body members; Secure business unit refused through the named resolution; RuleSetSummary members.</step>
    <step order="3">OperationAccessPolicy key and the named-record endpoint checks; contract test for 403 without AppendTo.</step>
    <step order="4">Id-keyed routes (4.6): server-read core lookup, caller Read (+ AppendTo on writes) before any read-back or write, one uniform 404, List filtered through GetCallerRightsForRecordsAsync; RouteAuthorizationGuardTests basis per route; tests for each route.</step>
    <step order="5">Q9 lock in AssignAsync; Draft re-scope built like InvoiceDocumentRefile (503 on a failed isolation read, conditional lookup write in applyChange, IsNotPermitted-only 403 mapping, RecordOwnerRefused for the rest, AfterRefileAsync only when !ParentsUnchanged); RefileWriterAfterRefileGuardTests entry.</step>
    <step order="6">Owner routing from each row's own lookups at the three create sites; RuleSetServiceOwnerTests (set [core], policy [set], version [policy]); the #2150 refusal path test.</step>
    <step order="6a">The source document (D-145): unlinked and caller-BU-owned for ClientDefault / Firm; filed under the record through its typed lookup, owned from its own row, stored in the record's container, own Access Permission Restricted for Record / FirmRecord; census UnscannedWriters row for the CreateDocumentAsync seam caller; tests.</step>
    <step order="7">The secure family in one change: lineage (entity set sprk_rulesets), OwnershipParentEntities, OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES and SecureChildNewCommandAgreementTests, StampedChildTables + Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 ($SolutionHomes, secure and verify only) + its Pester pin, role JSON row (evidence filled in step 9), census (ChildTables, Routed, PersonBearingWriters, UnscannedWriters, waiver deleted), narrower guard and twin guard (with seeding proofs), the separate non-throwing NFR-05 list and SecureBuRoleDepthAssertionTests, SecureChildLineageTests, SecureFamilyConsistencyTests, the three-hop reconciler test; check the three root main forms for a Rule Set subgrid (081.2).</step>
    <step order="8">Read live, read-only: sprk_ruleset's OwnershipType (must be UserOwned); the role(s) holding prvWritesprk_ruleset and every non-admin role's Read depth on the three tables; the privilege names' schema casing.</step>
    <step order="9">With the owner's OK: the live refusal probe (record the verbatim refusal in the role JSON evidence); Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1 -WhatIf / -Apply / -Verify; Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 dry run / -Apply / -Verify; the live NFR-05 run. Notices to uac-r2 before and after.</step>
    <step order="10">D-146: nothing to send uac-r2 for delete (no citation check). Record in the task notes that the delete job keeps and unlinks the set and never re-owns it, and that retire / re-scope of an orphaned set is the known limit in design note 4.5.</step>
    <step order="11">dotnet build; dotnet test (unit, ArchTests, contract, the data-mutation agreement test); the Pester pin (tests/scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.Tests.ps1); the client package test that holds OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES; publish-size delta; /conflict-check.</step>
    <step order="12">Reviews: uac-r2 (lineage, resolver list, client list, role row and probe, creator-person rows and script, the separate NFR-05 list, re-scope sequence, id-keyed checks, the source-document filing), ontology-r1 (guards; creator-person rows on sprk_policy and sprk_policyversion). Record both.</step>
    <step order="13">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="14">Record deviations in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/081-ruleset-scope-service.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any part of the secure-family change (lineage, OwnershipParentEntities, OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES, role row, creator-person rows and Pester pin, census, the NFR-05 list) cannot land in the same PR as the others, STOP: a subset fails SecureFamilyConsistencyTests, SecureChildNewCommandAgreementTests or the census, and shipping it piecemeal is what uac-r2 forbade.</trigger>
    <trigger>If #2150 (was #2143) has not merged to master, STOP and ask the main session; do not build on the unconditional reparent write.</trigger>
    <trigger>If UAC T7 has not merged, STOP: a filed source document on a matter with partner grants would be visible to those partners (D-145).</trigger>
    <trigger>If sprk_createdbyperson is missing on sprk_ruleset (080) or on sprk_policy / sprk_policyversion (ontology-r1), STOP: Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 never creates it for a $SolutionHomes table and its -Apply reports FAIL. Do not add a create to uac-r2's script.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a Draft re-scope of a set whose source document is filed under the old record needs the document re-filed or its file moved between containers, and no existing re-file path does both, STOP and agree the shape with uac-r2 and the main session; do not leave the document under the old record silently.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the refusal probe's create SUCCEEDS (the Secure Record Owner role already reads sprk_ruleset), delete the probe row, record it and STOP: the role JSON's evidence rule cannot be met as written; ask uac-r2.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the live NFR-05 run reports any non-admin role whose Read on sprk_ruleset, sprk_policy or sprk_policyversion reaches the Secure business unit (including the billing admins' role), STOP and raise 🔔 Human Input Required: a Secure-team owner would hide nothing, and changing a role is uac-r2's and the owner's call.</trigger>
    <trigger>If sprk_ruleset's live OwnershipType is not UserOwned, STOP: OwnershipParentEntities requires it.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the owner has not given the OK for the probe and the two -Apply runs, do not run them; finish the code, keep the role row's evidence empty only in a local branch, do not open the PR, and report.</trigger>
    <trigger>If ontology-r1 or uac-r2 rejects a guard, the twin guard, the lineage change, the creator-person rows, the NFR-05 list shape or the re-scope sequence in review, STOP; do not weaken a guard to make it pass.</trigger>
    <trigger>If routing through the resolver or the re-scope needs a resolver change in RecordOwnershipResolver beyond adding sprk_ruleset to OwnershipParentEntities, STOP and ask uac-r2.</trigger>
    <trigger>If an id-keyed route cannot run the record check before its first read-back or write (for example a filter that has no access to the set's lookup), STOP and agree the shape with uac-r2; do not fall back to the billing-admin privilege alone.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>RuleSetService, RuleSetEndpoints and the 076 validation exist and are extended; OperationAccessPolicy has finance.read (Read) and finance.submit_invoice (Read | AppendTo); the census, SecureChildLineage, the role JSON, StampedChildTables and OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES already list sprk_policy (or its peers); the F3 re-file sequence exists in InvoiceDocumentRefile; the uniform 404 exists (FinanceAuthorizationFilter.UniformRecordNotFound); the batched rights probe exists (CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerRightsForRecordsAsync); sprk_document is already in the lineage, the role set, the census seam and the creator-person tables, so filing the source document adds no UAC surface.</existing>
    <extension>All behaviour extends existing files and lists. One new operation key, because neither existing key names this act (a deny would read "submit invoice", the precedent noted in OperationAccessPolicy). One new guard test file and one new reconciler test file hold the two new controls. The NFR-05 change is a second list beside GuardedPrivileges, not a change to it, because the existing list's throw-on-missing contract is what protects the three roots.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A matter-scoped rule set cannot be created; if it were, a caller without AppendTo could attach terms to any record, a billing admin could read or change a Secure matter's set by its id, a Draft re-scope could pull a set out of Secure without F3, a Secure matter's set, policies and versions would sit in the ordinary business unit, its source document would be stranded outside the wall (never moved by Step 8, the reconciler or Unsecure), and every Record-scoped create on a Secure matter would fail with 0x80040299.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test</tool>
    <tool name="pwsh">Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1, Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 (owner OK); Invoke-Pester for the script pin</tool>
    <tool name="npm">the Spaarke.UI.Components test that holds OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES</tool>
    <tool name="dataverse-mcp">live role and metadata reads; the refusal probe (owner OK)</tool>
    <tool name="conflict-check">before the PR</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">RuleSetService.cs, RuleSetEndpoints.cs, OperationAccessPolicy.cs, SecureChildLineage.cs, RecordOwnershipResolver.cs, RecordCreatorPerson.cs, SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion.cs, bffChildWriteAdapter.ts, config/secure-record-owner-role.json, scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1</output>
    <output type="test">the test files listed in relevant-files, including tests/scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.Tests.ps1</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/081-ruleset-scope-service.md (probe evidence, -Apply / -Verify output, NFR-05 result, OwnershipType read, the D-146 note)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Each row of the 4.1 matrix has one passing test for its field error on create, assign and publish; a valid Record and FirmRecord set is created and published.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A caller without AppendTo on a core record named in the request gets 403 from the filter and nothing is written; a caller with Read + AppendTo passes (contract test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Id-keyed routes: for each route, an unknown set id and a set whose core record the caller cannot Read return byte-identical 404s, and no Dataverse write and no set field is returned (negative); a write route with Read but without AppendTo returns the same 404; a ClientDefault / Firm set passes with the billing-admin privilege alone; a Record set with no core lookup owned by the Secure team returns the same 404 to a billing admin who cannot Read the set row (negative) and is returned to one who can; List omits a set whose record the caller cannot Read and keeps one they can, with one GetCallerRightsForRecordsAsync call per page (no per-row loop); RouteAuthorizationGuardTests fails when a route's declared basis is removed (seeding proof).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Changing scope, firm, core record or BU list of a Published set (Firm included) returns 409 ruleset.scope_locked and writes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Draft re-scope: off a Secure matter without the caller's F3 right → 403 sdap.unsecure.not_permitted and no write (negative); with it → ReparentAsync is called once, on the set only, the lookups are written conditionally on the set's version, then AfterRefileAsync("sprk_ruleset", id, ...) runs, and the reconciler test shows the policies and versions re-owned; RefileWriterAfterRefileGuardTests fails if the AfterRefileAsync call is removed (seeding proof).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Draft re-scope negatives: a failed isolation read returns 503 and writes nothing; an unresolved team is NOT 403 not_permitted (it is RecordOwnerRefused's status and code); a concurrent change of the set's row (version mismatch) refuses and writes nothing; the #2150 typed refusal maps through RecordOwnerRefused; a re-scope whose parents are unchanged does not call AfterRefileAsync.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish with AllBusinessUnits No and an empty list returns ruleset.publish_invalid with field businessUnits; a list with an unknown business unit, or with the Secure Record business unit, is refused; an ambiguous Secure business-unit resolution refuses the write (negative: never accepted).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Owner parents: a record-scoped set create passes exactly [core record]; its policy create exactly [the set]; its version create exactly [the policy] (never [core record]); a Secure matter yields the Secure team as owner of all three; a client-default set create passes none; a resolver refusal writes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Source document (D-145): a ClientDefault or Firm set's document has no core lookup, lives in the Procedure Library and is owned by the caller's business-unit team with no parent; a Record or FirmRecord set's document carries exactly the set's core record in its typed lookup, its owner resolution is called with exactly [that record] read from the document row (negative: never the set's owner passed in), its file goes to the record's container (negative: never the Procedure Library), and its sprk_accesspermission is Restricted; the census lists RuleSetService in UnscannedWriters as a CreateDocumentAsync seam caller.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The census lists sprk_policy, sprk_policyversion and sprk_ruleset as Routed, RuleSetServicePolicyWaiver is gone, PersonBearingWriters has the RuleSetService entry; EveryRoutedEntryRoutesThroughTheResolver, EveryChildTableTheServerCreatesCarriesTheCreatorPersonColumn and EveryAppCreateWriterThatActsForAPersonNamesThem pass; ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchemaAgreementTests and the Pester pin pass with the three tables, each a $SolutionHomes table (the script secures and verifies, never creates).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SecureFamilyConsistencyTests passes with sprk_ruleset in the lineage (entity set sprk_rulesets), the role JSON and the census; SecureChildNewCommandAgreementTests passes with sprk_ruleset in OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES; removing sprk_ruleset from any one of them fails the matching test (seeding proof).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The three root main forms have no Rule Set subgrid, or the one that exists is in ChildSubgridsOnMainForms and served by the secure-child ribbon (recorded with the form ids).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The narrower guard fails on a planted policy["sprk_matter"] write and passes on ruleSet["sprk_matter"]; the twin guard fails on a planted sprk_ruleset write in OntologyAdminAuthoringService; each has a recorded seeding proof.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The SecureChildReconciler test covers version → policy → ruleset → core on secure and on unsecure; SecureChildLineageTests include sprk_ruleset.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NFR-05: GuardedPrivileges is unchanged (still exactly the three roots, and SecureBuRoleDepthAssertionTests' pin unchanged); the separate list covers the three billing tables; a census read missing prvReadsprk_ruleset still grades clauses 1-4 and reports exactly one finding naming it (negative: the census is not thrown away); a non-admin role with Deep or Global Read on sprk_ruleset reaching the Secure business unit is reported, one with Basic is not; the live NFR-05 run on dev is recorded with no finding on the three tables.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Notes record: the probe's verbatim refusal (also in the role JSON evidence), the -Apply and -Verify outputs of both scripts, the owner's OK with dates, sprk_ruleset's live OwnershipType (UserOwned), and the D-146 note. No delete-Restrict, no delete code and no Retire logic is added, and no citing-lookup list is sent for delete (negative).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta recorded; no new package; no new HIGH CVE; /conflict-check run.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Two adversarial-review passes (auth, tenant-isolation). The applicability predicate (RuleSetApplicability) is 082's, not this task's. The Rule Review UI is 084's. Rate cards join the secure family in 086 (after this task, same files). The Secure business-unit snapshot writer is 087's. The role row and the creator-person column must be live on dev before 079 deploys the BFF; 079 re-runs -Verify on both, and the release path does the same in every other environment. D-146: the delete job unlinks and never re-owns, so a set under a Secure matter stays Secure-owned after the delete; retire / re-scope of such orphans by billing admins is a known limit (design note 4.5), not R1 work. #2151 (UAC): the strict derived-container rule has no case for the Procedure Library or the e-Billing output container; settle it before DocumentPointer:StrictDerivedContainer is turned on where ebilling is deployed.</notes>

